  ],
  "text": "You have never seen a whole rainbow. The ground cuts off the bottom half. A rainbow is not in the sky. It is not anywhere. Sunlight enters a raindrop, bends, bounces off the back, and bends again on the way out. Each colour bends by a slightly different amount, so they leave separated. And they all leave at almost exactly forty two degrees from the direction you are looking. Which means the rainbow is a shape drawn around your own shadow. It is a full circle. From the ground you only ever get the top of it. From an aircraft, with nothing in the way, you can see the whole ring. And nobody else is seeing yours. Their circle is built from entirely different droplets. You cannot walk to it, because it is not an object. It is an angle. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
